# scaleup_single_switch_72_3600Gbps.topo
#
# Models an NVLink-class SCALE-UP domain as a single non-blocking crossbar:
# 72 hosts (GPUs) all attached to ONE ToR switch, every pair exactly one hop apart.
# This is the CURRENT-GENERATION REAL-HARDWARE anchor: the GB200 NVL72 places 72
# Blackwell GPUs in one NVLink domain behind a single NVSwitch tier (one hop, fully
# non-blocking, 1800 GB/s per GPU). Modelled here at the sweep's uniform 3600 Gbps
# per-host NVLink-aggregate class; switch latency 300 ns, link 500 ns.
#
# Encoding note: htsim's FatTree parser rejects Tiers=1 (fat_tree_topology.cpp), so a
# single switch is expressed as a DEGENERATE 2-tier fat-tree: Podsize == Nodes and
# Tier-0 Radix_Down == Nodes => exactly one ToR holds all hosts. The Tier-1 uplink
# (Radix_Up 1) is vestigial and carries no host<->host traffic (all pairs are same-ToR,
# one hop). Oversubscribed == Nodes keeps radix_down/radix_up == oversub (parser check).
#
# Sibling of scaleup_single_switch_{2..64}_3600Gbps.topo, scaled to 72 hosts (NVL72) for
# the INC-vs-ring speedup-vs-N sweep (D3). NOTE: 72 is NOT a power of two, so the
# recursive-doubling arm is skipped for this N (ring is the endpoint baseline).
Nodes 72
Tiers 2
Podsize 72

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 3600
Radix_Down 72
Radix_Up 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 500
Switch_Latency_ns 300
Oversubscribed 72

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 3600
Radix_Down 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 500
Switch_Latency_ns 300
